//? Title: Graph coloring: first fit is feasible, not necessarily few
//? Subtitle: Actual degree order, blocked-color probes and a bipartite counterexample
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Given pairwise conflicts, assign a label to every vertex so conflicting vertices
receive different labels. Fewer labels can mean fewer time slots or
interchangeable resources, but a valid assignment need not minimize that count.
Degree-ordered first fit chooses the smallest unblocked color at each vertex.
This report follows actual native decisions on the original five-cycle and
complete four-vertex graph, proves the degree bound, and constructs bipartite
crown graphs where deterministic tie order spends arbitrarily many colors
despite a two-color witness. Explicit multigraph, loop-deletion and verifier
controls state precisely which constraints the implementation solves.
)

\toc

> Watch the last vertex of the five-cycle

The original cycle \(C_5\) has edges 0–1–2–3–4–0. Every degree is two, so
descending degree with ascending-ID ties visits 0,1,2,3,4. The first four
vertices alternate colors zero and one. The final vertex sees both colors and
must choose two. The table records the actual producing assignments and the
final availability probes, including the first free slot.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/coloring_cycle.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto g = dm::algorithms::coloring_cycle(5);
    const auto t = dm::algorithms::greedy_coloring_trace(g.vertices, g.edges);
    const auto &a = t.analysis;
    std::print("| visit | vertex | multigraph degree | assigned color |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < a.order.size(); ++i) {
        const auto v = a.order[i];
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", i, v, a.degree[v],
                   a.result.color[v]);
    }
    std::print("\n| final vertex | tested color | blocked |\n| ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &e : t.events)
        if (e.vertex == 4 && e.action == dm::algorithms::ColoringAction::probe)
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} |\n", e.vertex, e.color, e.flag);
    std::print("\nColors {}; projected graph proper {}; degree ceiling {}; neighbor visits {}; color probes " "{}; assignments {}.\n",
               a.result.num_colors,
               dm::algorithms::is_proper_coloring(g.vertices, g.edges,
                                                  a.result.color),
               a.work.max_degree + 1, a.work.neighbor_visits,
               a.work.color_probes, a.work.assignments);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d =
        dm::algorithms::coloring_diagram(g, a.result,
                                         "Actual first-fit coloring of C5");
    d.text({0, -4.4}, "v4: color 0 blocked, color 1 blocked, color 2 free", 22).save_svg("build/coloring_cycle.svg");
    if (a.result.color != std::vector<std::size_t>{0, 1, 0, 1, 2})
        throw std::runtime_error("original cycle");
}
```
