> Count actual work and trace records

Let n be vertices and m the nonloop edge records, counting duplicates. The
adjacency list contains 2m entries and the sweep visits every entry once.
Initializing degree(v)+1 availability slots at every vertex totals n+2m slots.
Each chosen color c(v) takes c(v)+1 marker reads, including the free one:

$$A=2m,\qquad S=n+2m,\qquad
P=\sum_v(c(v)+1)\le S,\qquad
H=A+P+n\le4m+2n.$$
\alttext(Adjacency visits are twice the nonloop record count. Marker slots total n plus twice that count. Probe reads include the first free color, and the optional trace adds one event per visit, probe and assignment.)

Here H counts actual neighbor, probe and assignment records. Marker writes may
repeat the same slot for parallel edges; every actual write is counted. Sorting
adds O(n log n) comparisons, and original edge validation/preparation visits
loops too. Overall work is O(n log n+original edge records), with O(n+m)
working/output storage and O(n+m) optional trace. These are logical counts, not
timing, allocator or machine-instruction measurements.

For the paired crown, colors i occur twice for i=0,...,k−1, so P=k(k+1) and
H=3k²+k. Grouped IDs give P=3k and H=2k²+3k. Both graphs have the same edge
count. The next sweep checks these formulas against actual native records; only
the palette is plotted.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/coloring_scaling.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    std::print("| pairs k | vertices | edge records | paired palette | grouped palette | paired probes | " "grouped probes | paired history |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: " "|\n");
    std::vector<double> x, paired, grouped;
    for (std::size_t k : {2, 3, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32}) {
        const auto p =
            dm::algorithms::coloring_crown(k, true), g =
            dm::algorithms::coloring_crown(k, false);
        const auto a =
            dm::algorithms::greedy_coloring_trace(p.vertices, p.edges), b =
            dm::algorithms::greedy_coloring_trace(g.vertices, g.edges);
        const auto &u = a.analysis.work;
        const auto &v = b.analysis.work;
        if (a.analysis.result.num_colors != k ||
            b.analysis.result.num_colors != 2 ||
            u.neighbor_visits != 2 * k * (k - 1) ||
            u.marker_slots != 2 * k * k || u.color_probes != k * (k + 1) ||
            v.color_probes != 3 * k || a.events.size() != 3 * k * k + k ||
            b.events.size() != 2 * k * k + 3 * k)
            throw std::runtime_error("crown counts");
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", k, p.vertices,
                   p.edges.size(), a.analysis.result.num_colors,
                   b.analysis.result.num_colors, u.color_probes, v.color_probes,
                   a.events.size());
        x.push_back(k);
        paired.push_back(a.analysis.result.num_colors);
        grouped.push_back(b.analysis.result.num_colors);
    }
    auto plot = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    plot.line(x, paired, "paired IDs", {37, 99, 235}, 2).points(x, paired, "",
                                                                {37, 99, 235}, 4).line(x, grouped, "grouped IDs = optimum", {220, 38, 38}, 2).title("Same crown graphs, different degree-tie numbering").x_label("matched pairs k").y_label("actual greedy colors").y_limits(0, 40).save_svg("build/coloring_scaling.svg");
}
